        "subject": "LU-18652 tests: re-enable conf-sanity/108a on ZFS",
        "message": "LU-18652 tests: re-enable conf-sanity/108a on ZFS\n\nSince OpenZFS 2.2 setting the mountpoint of a canmount=on dataset\nalso mounts it, so the explicit \"zfs mount\" in test_108a fails with\n\"filesystem already mounted\". Use canmount=noauto so only the\nexplicit mount happens, and drop 108a from the always_except list.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=108a fstype=zfs\nSigned-off-by: Robert Read <rread@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I94226219db060fbaaf06fd98b569c13947633ddd\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68465\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Arshad Hussain <arshad.hussain@aeoncomputing.com>\nReviewed-by: Jian Yu <yujian@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
